    "about_lede": "The pictures are inventions, or reinventions of reality. Sometimes they may appear a little awkward and strange, but it is their awkwardness that gives them the power to communicate.",
    "about_text": "Richard Sorrell was born in 1948, the son of the historical draughtsman and painter Alan Sorrell and the watercolourist Elizabeth Sorrell. He studied at Walthamstow Art School, Kingston College of Art and the Royal Academy Schools.\n\nFor around 25 years, living in London and Norfolk, he painted landscape, still life and portraits, and became known for aerial views of great houses for the National Trust and private owners. Over the past two decades the invented paintings have come to the fore, alongside an interest in sculpture, gardens and planting.\n\nHe was elected to the Royal Watercolour Society in 1975 and served as its President from 2006 to 2009.",
